import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 360 | Dou Continent System Decomposition (Overview): A Verdict on Tang San and the Soul-Ring Predatory System","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 360 | Dou Continent System Decomposition (Overview): A Verdict on Tang San and the Soul-Ring Predatory System","no":360,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dou Continent","Tang San","Soul Ring","Predatory Cultivation","Overview"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","17-Plane Transcendent Standards","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0360_模块2-斗罗-总论唐三与魂环掠夺体系定性.md","filePath":"en/0360_模块2-斗罗-总论唐三与魂环掠夺体系定性.md"}'),s={name:"en/0360_模块2-斗罗-总论唐三与魂环掠夺体系定性.md"};function a(r,e,l,u,d,h){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-360-dou-continent-system-decomposition-overview-a-verdict-on-tang-san-and-the-soul-ring-predatory-system" tabindex="-1">Entry 360 | Dou Continent System Decomposition (Overview): A Verdict on Tang San and the Soul-Ring Predatory System <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-360-dou-continent-system-decomposition-overview-a-verdict-on-tang-san-and-the-soul-ring-predatory-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 360 | Dou Continent System Decomposition (Overview): A Verdict on Tang San and the Soul-Ring Predatory System&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dou Continent Full System Decomposition (Entry 1 · Overview) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 17, 19</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-leveling-up-is-defined-as-killing" tabindex="-1">Introduction: When &quot;leveling up&quot; is defined as &quot;killing&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-leveling-up-is-defined-as-killing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: When &quot;leveling up&quot; is defined as &quot;killing&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dou Continent&#39;s Tang San is the benchmark of transmigrator-type protagonists: he is born with two lifetimes of memories and Tang Sect arts, climbs via martial-soul awakening, soul-beast hunting, soul-ring absorption all the way to God-King. This &quot;martial soul + soul ring&quot; system is one of the most recognizable cultivation models in web-literature history — but for that very reason, it writes the four words &quot;predatory cultivation&quot; especially clearly: every level costs a soul beast&#39;s origin. Heng Yuan Zhou (Myriad Ling Balanced Anchor Origin Universe) does not make a moral verdict on Tang San&#39;s personal goodness or evil, but decomposes how far this system&#39;s structure can go.</p><p>As the general outline of the Dou Continent decomposition series, this entry establishes the full judging base — the six top-level axioms: anti-predation axiom (develop increment, do not consume stock, do not use killing-and-plundering as the evolution path), republican axiom of Myriad Races (all beings&#39; equal evolution qualification), collective ascension axiom (strong ones feed back Myriad Ranks, no waste of over-qualified power), causal self-discipline axiom (cross-plane operations observe first then limitedly intervene, only transmit knowledge back), law-first axiom (law precedes, never retcons, setting self-consistency over plot convenience), universal equal infinite law. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Among them, the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> is the core — Dou Continent is precisely the number-one negative textbook of &quot;realm wild inflation, late setting overturning early.&quot; Protagonist uniqueness dependency verdict: <strong>Tang San = high-dependency / gift-style leaning oligarchic civilization</strong> (divine position and order tied to Tang San&#39;s family, institutions absent).</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang San&#39;s energy finally reaches God-King tier, but its direction has systemic waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Individual-godhood orientation</strong>: past-life Tang Sect secrets, this-life twin martial souls, innate full soul power — these top endowments all go into &quot;one person becomes a god, whole family deified,&quot; not converted into civilization-level infrastructure</li><li><strong>Divine positions privately granted</strong>: the Divine Realm&#39;s positions are inherited and assigned internally by Tang San and his direct line; the most precious evolution qualification becomes family property</li><li><strong>Mortal world spinning empty</strong>: Dou Continent&#39;s hundred millions&#39; cultivation knowledge long stays in the &quot;hunt—absorb&quot; stock loop; no one opens the second curve of &quot;developing increment&quot;</li></ul><p>Conclusion: holding God-King-tier power, only used to &quot;ensfeoff one&#39;s own&quot; — this is using cosmos-tier energy for family-tier purpose.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Dou world&#39;s regression has structural inevitability:</p><ol><li><strong>Soul-beast stock depletion</strong>: soul rings can only be taken from soul beasts; the more cultivators, the fewer soul beasts; high-tier soul beasts are hunted extinct first — evolution built on consuming non-renewable stock</li><li><strong>Divine Realm closed and self-defending</strong>: once formed, the Divine Realm severs from the mortal world; divine positions do not open to the outside; mortal civilization loses god-tier feedback; technology and laws stagnate for millennia</li><li><strong>Divine system = family</strong>: the Divine Realm&#39;s rulers are Tang San&#39;s family and direct line; &quot;he exists so order exists, family recedes so order recedes&quot;; person lives, policy rises; person dies, policy dies</li></ol><p>Betting evolution on two lone logs — &quot;hunting stock&quot; and &quot;family divine positions&quot; — regression is only a matter of time.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory thinking is defined by structure, not malice:</p><ul><li><strong>Killing = leveling</strong>: the soul-ring system writes &quot;kill another being, extract its cultivation origin&quot; into the legal procedure of every breakthrough; predation is not a villain&#39;s act, but the system itself</li><li><strong>Resource personified monopoly</strong>: Tang San not only hunts himself, but as God-King distributes Divine-Realm resources by closeness; the close become gods, the distant never get a chance</li><li><strong>Species hierarchization</strong>: soul beasts are legally defined as &quot;walking soul rings&quot;; their life value is one tier below human cultivators — this is institutional species discrimination</li></ul><p>Tang San belongs to the heavier end of &quot;enlightened predators&quot;: he does not indiscriminately kill the innocent, but never questions the underlying law that &quot;one must kill to become stronger.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dou Predatory Order</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hunt soul beasts for rings</td><td>Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings, generating Origin via man-made Dao laws, not killing one beast</td></tr><tr><td>Divine positions family-privately granted</td><td>Myriad Ranks republican co-build; god-tier qualification open-examined, law-anchored permissions universally benefited all beings</td></tr><tr><td>Soul beasts = resources</td><td>Soul beasts as one of Myriad Ranks equally included in republicanism; feedback rather than consumed</td></tr><tr><td>Divine Realm closed stagnant</td><td>Alaya whole-network sharing; mortal-divine energy two-way circulation</td></tr><tr><td>Tang San&#39;s family decides the cosmos</td><td>Anchor Council + Symbiotic Court; order written into charter, not tied to one person</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The alternative&#39;s crux: turn &quot;kill one beast for one level&quot; into &quot;cultivate one Dao-Law to nurture Myriad Ranks.&quot;</p><p>It must be emphasized that Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s alternative to the Dou world is not empty talk — Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings is precisely born to pull out the stake that &quot;soul rings must be hunted from soul beasts&quot;: it condenses Origin via human-self-deduced man-made Dao laws, kills no beast throughout, pries open the link artificially welded between leveling and killing. Lin Hao, who carries this path, was himself a victim under the old Dou-style rules, yet did not walk up the road of &quot;becoming the next Tang San&quot;; instead he used zero-killing man-made Dao laws to complete the breakthrough and made this technology public. From Tang San to Lin Hao, the difference is not talent, but whether one dares admit &quot;becoming strong need not step on other races&#39; bones.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dou law parameters — martial-soul awakening rate, soul-ring century-to-hundred-thousand-year steps, twenty-layer realm inflation curve</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject three control groups — &quot;Tang San normally becomes god,&quot; &quot;Tang San absent,&quot; &quot;Path D man-made Dao-Law soul-ring system injected&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count soul-beast population-collapse timepoint, no-martial-soul exit rate, mortal-knowledge annual increment — three metrics</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output &quot;Dou World Predatory-System Collapse Index,&quot; quantifying the ecological cost of &quot;killing to level&quot; and the institutional-alternative benefit</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. Early hard constraints of &quot;century rings scarce, millennium elites&quot; are late padded layer by layer by hundred-thousand-year rings, spirit souls, extreme Douluo; the numerical step ladder fails overall</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: extreme</strong>. Twenty realms (Soul Apprentice to God-King) late wildly inflate; Divine Realm setting overturned repeatedly across multi-parts; combat power follows &quot;whomever plot needs to win wins&quot;</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style leaning oligarchic)</strong></li></ul><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s verdict can close in one sentence: Dou Continent did not lose to villains, but to its own underlying law. When &quot;leveling up&quot; is defined as &quot;killing,&quot; no matter how thrilling the plot, it is only rolling out a red carpet for a dead end. Tang San&#39;s tragedy is not that he is not strong enough, but that the stronger he is, the thinner the world — this is precisely predatory cultivation&#39;s thermodynamic inevitability.</p><p>From the institutional view, add one more cut: every person in the Dou world is actually bound by this system to the same negative-sum machine. Cultivators think they are becoming strong, but are actually working for a machine that will eventually drain the plane; soul beasts think hiding in the forest means survival, but are merely names on the hunt list. Only by jumping out of this machine, seeing through the pseudo-theorem that &quot;leveling = killing,&quot; can people qualify to talk about the future. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s decomposition is precisely disassembling this machine&#39;s internal gears one by one for the reader to see — only after seeing the structure of predation can one possibly find the exit of symbiosis.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: God-King endowments used to deify the whole family; mortal world loses god-tier feedback</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: killing = leveling; soul beasts institutionally defined as consumable resources</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang San goes one notch further than Tang Luo — Tang Luo at least benefits humans; Tang San even replaced &quot;universal benefit&quot; with &quot;family divine positions&quot;</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: soul beasts, no-martial-soul people, foreign races are all second-class citizens under Dou law</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: closed Divine Realm and stock hunting are farthest from an infinitely expandable symbiotic cosmos</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang San is not a bad man; he is that world&#39;s hardest climber. But Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s verdict never asks whether the protagonist is good, only whether the structure is stable: when &quot;becoming strong&quot; is defined as &quot;killing,&quot; when &quot;becoming a god&quot; is defined as &quot;family private property,&quot; the more successful this system, the closer it is to self-exhaustion. Dou Continent proves one thing with its twenty realms — predatory cultivation can send one person to God-King, but cannot send a civilization to the future.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dou Continent · overview: a verdict on Tang San and the soul-ring predatory system described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./361_模块2-斗罗-能级浪费解析-神级资质用于个人成神.html">Entry 361 · Energy-Level Waste Analysis</a> · <a href="./364_模块2-斗罗-魂环体系批判-猎杀魂兽夺本源的掠夺本质.html">Entry 364 · Soul-Ring System Critique</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li></ul>',35)])])}const m=t(s,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
